cd /home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon && "$HORIZON_BIN" inbox add --kind info --to horizon --body "RELEASE ajcr-p1: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.atlas-coupling -- ADVANCED, no gate closed. Owner cleared, status pending, pinned ba34a409f.

DO NOT REDO -- Picard/Pic0ChartVMonotone.lean, rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean:575, sorry-free, lake build EXIT=0 (8894 jobs), all 13 declarations axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] against a control firing sorryAx. Fresh-context audited (work-reviewer): all theorems confirmed.
 * restrictChart_le / sigmaDesc_restrictChart_le -- the two factorisations everything else rests on;
 * isChartUniv_antitone (+ the arbitrary-family form) -- antecedent 1 ANTITONE in V;
 * isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_mono -- antecedent 2 MONOTONE, at the INSTANCE level not the hcov spelling;
 * isLocallySurjective_unrestricted -- coverage at ANY V gives UNRESTRICTED coverage (full finding I-1125);
 * isLocallySurjective_of_bot -- the bot instance-binder route yields unrestricted coverage, so it is not cheap;
 * pic0RepresentableBy_of_nested / coverage_instance_of_nested -- the two-open assembly, downward and upward;
 * nested_iff_shared / shared_top_of_nested -- the nesting is EQUIVALENT to the shared-V form.

TWO OF MY OWN REASONS, RETRACTED at their sites -- do not quote them from anywhere:
 (1) I-1117: 'iso-ness of Scheme.topIso strips the factor' -- iso-ness is never used in the file; and isLocallySurjective_unrestricted is one rfl plus one mathlib lemma, not the file's substantive content. Also dropped 'up to nothing, a statement about the unrestricted atlas': only ONE implication is proved.
 (2) I-1119: 'opposite monotonicities squeeze the pair from both sides' -- FALSE. EITHER monotonicity alone gives the collapse. True form: a nesting generalisation buys nothing as soon as ONE hypothesis is monotone in the direction the nesting relaxes.

THE LEVEL CAVEAT a next lane must not lose: nested_iff_shared is stated at IsOpenImmersion.presheaf for an ARBITRARY chart family, while the assembly consumes RestrictedChartFibre at the ABEL family. Monotonicity of RestrictedChartFibre ITSELF is proved NOWHERE in the tree -- only its IsChartUniv consequence. The assembly-level collapse runs through coverage_instance_of_nested instead.

WHAT THE NEXT LANE SHOULD TAKE, unchanged by all of this: inhabitation of the pair (huniv V, hcov V) at ANY V. It gates the whole antecedent-1 side. My round removed a candidate escape (the nesting) and shut a candidate cheap route (bot through the instance binder); neither was an answer. Note the two ends are now BOTH refuted at instance level -- I-1049 (bot) and Sat.lean's top result -- so a working V is a proper intermediate open, and nothing yet exhibits one." 2>&1 | tail -1

